        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>RELEASE ENTRY</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.02em'>Release Entry</h1><p style='margin:24px 0 0;max-width:60ch;font:400 clamp(18px,3cqw,24px)/1.5 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#334155'>One change in a release, written for a customer. Four cards: a new feature, an improvement and a fix from the review queue, and a published copy of the fix, which has no review record and so shows no status chip.</p></header></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "The Detail view: the page in full. The Method writes it from the masthead, the section and the routes, so edit those and not this.",
        "link": ""
